WEBVTT

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.420
That's what Kiyoko was trying to tell you?

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:52.180
Yeah...

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.030
What does "Cleansing Flood" mean?

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:58.290
A great flood that washes everything clean...

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.400
Now that you say that, recently I get the feeling somehow...

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:04.270
...that the mirror in the sky has been descending, huh?

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:22.080
That thing Reiko's wearing... Did you lend it to her?

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.090
Do you mean the sleeved apron?

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:27.250
Yes; we can't have Reiko's clothing becoming soiled.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.560
So it's called a sleeved apron.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:31.590
It's very becoming, isn't it?

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.430
Yeah...

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:37.330
But hey, her being able to use Dynamis...

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.500
I wonder if that means she's somebody's clone?

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:41.560
You didn't know, Master Toru?

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.070
You know?

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.170
Yes, well...

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.740
You are aware of the reason Reiko is blind now, correct?

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:50.420
She gave her eyes to Chairman Yuki, right?

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.110
Because she felt sorry for him, she said.

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:58.080
I'm sure you can understand that for that purpose, the two of them needed to be a genetic match.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:01.820
It can't be...

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:05.420
Yes, Reiko is Chairman Yuki's clone, Master Toru.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.460
So that means she's a bo...

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.290
That is correct.

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.410
Good morning.

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:16.600
Good morning!

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.040
Good morning.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.940
Shall we help with something?

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.940
Well, could I ask you to carry the plates?

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.580
Yes!

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.210
Hey, Toru! You help too!

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:33.890
Hey, well, he said Reiko is a boy.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:36.020
Huh? Is there something the matter with that?

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:40.260
What? You didn't know?

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:45.100
Isamu, did you know? About Reiko...

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.430
He's a boy, right?

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:52.370
Tatsuya, did you know? That Reiko is a boy?

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:53.940
Yeah...

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:55.750
How come you knew?

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.510
Why? Because we're both guys.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:09.730
It's a lie. I can't believe it. No, I won't believe it!

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.560
Good morning, my lady.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:14.790
Good morning.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.600
Good morning, Ma'am.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.130
Thank you.

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.910
Why don't you join us as well?

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.620
No, my lady, it wouldn't be...

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:44.390
It's my wish that you do. And we're the only ones here.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.260
The food tastes better when everyone eats together.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.460
That's right.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:54.660
Thank you, my lady.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.070
Is it always like this?

00:05:33.910 --> 00:05:35.710
Everyone being so gloomy...

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:39.010
We're all gathered together, but it's no fun.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.380
No, it's not like that.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:45.320
That reminds me, what happened to Bu, your stuffed pig?

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:48.390
I left it at my family's house.

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:49.890
Your family's house?

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:54.630
At the family home of my original, Haruka Mayuzumi.

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:04.060
Fu...

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:19.250
Takaaki Kagami, Haruka Mayuzumi, Shouichi Kidokoro...

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:24.730
We went not just to mine, but also to the family homes of Fujisaki's and Toru's originals.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:29.800
They showed us photo albums, and gave us some pictures from them.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.930
Every one of those homes received us pleasantly.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:40.510
Even just by that, we knew right away that, yes, they were brought up with love.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:43.510
This is me...

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:49.940
You see, these are photos that show our originals.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:53.510
What are "originals"?

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:57.860
It's hard to explain, so later, okay?

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.790
Our look-alikes are in the pictures.

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.400
Is this you, Toru?

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.270
Right, when I was ten years old.

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:20.920
Isn't this you, my lady?

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.220
Huh? Which one, which one?

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:23.990
Oh, this girl?

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:26.150
It's true! I didn't notice!

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:28.250
This is also her.

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:30.390
You're so pretty!

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:32.200
No different now, either, huh?

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:34.220
Yeah, you look, like, intellectual.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:40.100
We brought a message from all those parents.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:45.060
They were all saying we should be certain to pass it on to you.

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:49.810
"Thank you for finding these children, and for raising them for us."

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:05.150
What we did at Heaven's Gate may have been wrong,

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:10.330
...since as a result we sowed the seeds of many tragedies.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:20.140
But I'm grateful from my very heart that I can dine together with all of you here and now.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:24.180
I feel so happy for this stroke of fortune.

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:29.440
Why are you saying that now?

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:36.660
I knew that a long time ago.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:40.390
That's why I came back here, right?

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:47.770
To me, who couldn't even write, you taught everything under the sun, and you gave me everything, right?

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:49.630
Fu...

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:54.330
Little Hiroko gave me a new birth when I was in tatters.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.510
You brought me into this world one more time.

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:23.840
You're all a family. It's wonderful, isn't it?

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:28.110
I don't really understand. Did they make up?

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:30.840
Yeah, let's leave it at that for now.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:32.820
That's good.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:38.050
Mightn't it be nice to take some photographs of all of you now?

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.360
Photos?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:43.960
Come to think of it, I don't have a single photo of all of you.

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:49.400
That would be lovely.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:50.590
Yeah...

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:17.330
Hey, wasn't going to your original's home scary?

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:20.800
At any rate, I wanted to help Fu get back on her feet.

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:23.390
I certainly was anxious before we went though.

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:25.770
But it's good that we went, huh?

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:30.610
Yeah, because by tracing our roots, we learned that there were a lot of good things too,

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:33.080
...and that we ourselves are what it all led to.

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:36.210
Have both of you two changed somehow?

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:38.880
It seems like you've become more mature.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:40.870
That's true for you too, Madoka.

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:42.190
Huh?

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:44.650
Protecting your sister from Little Hiroko...

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:46.960
I think maybe I've gotten a crush on you again.

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:51.520
Fu...

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:53.460
Just kidding.

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:57.760
That's funny. I don't get it, but...

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:00.300
Here goes!

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:01.830
You're here, okay?

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:06.840
Reiko, smile.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:19.780
Happy-go-lucky, aren't we?

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:23.560
At this critical time, you're taking a commemorative photo?

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:28.760
What's your business here? I don't remember inviting you.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:32.400
We're requisitioning this hotel.

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.100
Requisitioning?

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:45.320
Now that we've proven that their objective lies with all of you, it's only proper that we lay a net.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:47.920
If you're going to insist...

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:50.250
...shall I arrange for official papers?

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:53.150
No, there's no need.

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:57.400
I'll be establishing a temporary command center at this hotel.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:57.900
You will immediately...

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.420
That's all the orders you'll be giving.

00:12:00.300 --> 00:12:03.700
We will remain in this hotel, so proceed on that assumption.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.740
Beyond that, do as you like.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.770
I'm grateful for your cooperation.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.440
All right, everyone, go back to your rooms.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.140
Kiyoko's in the infirmary.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.150
It'll be bad if she's found by those guys!

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:44.070
I know this is sudden, but evacuate to a safe place and take this in for developing, if you would.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:49.240
If you've got this many photos, you can create an album, right?

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:56.050
When all this is over, come and bring it to us.

00:12:58.160 --> 00:12:59.180
I understand, my lady.

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:04.160
Be careful.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.030
See you again someday.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:09.630
Keep yourself safe too, my lady.

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:30.740
This room won't collapse from minor impacts.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:33.850
She'll be all right even if the Blattaria go on a rampage.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:36.320
Even a place like this can be useful, huh?

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:39.620
Tatsuya, she'll definitely be safe.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.130
Thanks, all of you.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:47.170
They're here.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:49.910
Ma...

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:07.390
Kiyoko, we should have taken some pictures, huh?

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:12.350
But...

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:17.190
Since we'll always be together...

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:42.880
Might you permit me to ask one thing?

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:46.350
It's about Tear.

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:47.790
Tear?

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:55.090
I'm aware that following XX, Delphys buried itself underground and became the cause of the Sheltering Sky.

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:58.090
So what do you suppose became of Tear?

00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:01.670
I would guess it's still inside Delphys even now.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.240
I can't conceive of Tear abiding anywhere else.

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:10.370
"Delphys is also linked to human hearts."

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:13.740
Those are the words of the man who was your lover, aren't they?

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:20.920
That being the case, I wonder if Enkidu is acting upon Delphys using his own mind?

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:26.220
"Terumichi Madoka isn't a person who would do that sort of thing."

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:29.760
The fact is, I also believe that.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:35.860
If that's so, then don't you suppose he's been beguiled, and is being manipulated by someone else?

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:38.240
You're saying that's Tear?

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:40.570
Absurd!

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:58.860
What's absurd is this war, since even if we win, I'm a war criminal,

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:02.290
...as of the moment I drew children into battle.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:07.300
I don't know whether it will be men or God who will judge me, but...

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.470
Well, you're likely guilty of the same crime too though.

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:13.170
You're right.

00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:22.180
Well then, shall I just become a god myself?

00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:24.670
What's wrong?

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:27.150
Madoka!

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:28.640
It's because of that machine!

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:39.020
Stop that device! Immediately!

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:43.090
I'm only carrying out my mission.

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:46.260
If you really insist, go ahead and do it by force.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:57.070
I'm grateful to young Tatsuya Madoka, since this new weapon was developed using his data.

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:00.150
You couldn't have... using that child's Dynamis...

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:05.920
Just as you have guessed, we thoroughly examined the wave Tatsuya Madoka emits.

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:09.480
Namely, that wave which is identical to Enkidu's.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:11.430
Do you intend to kill that child?!

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:15.730
It's for the sake of world peace. It can't be avoided.

00:19:20.700 --> 00:19:23.730
Go! Now is the time, wipe out Gilgamesh!

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:52.260
What's this?

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:06.110
What happened?

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.420
Are you all right?

00:20:09.420 --> 00:20:10.680
Yeah...

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:13.750
Something's coming!

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:16.850
Look up there!

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:28.960
Takaaki Kagami?!

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:36.870
Haruka Mayuzumi?!

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:42.210
Shouichi Kidokoro?!

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:44.620
All three of them are supposed to be dead!

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.240
Dr. Madoka!

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:05.980
How exciting! Enkidu!

00:21:06.510 --> 00:21:11.920
I've learned everything about you, from head to toe, using your cloned boy, that is.
